
 Moving Average Convergence Divergence
 ======================================

 Tells you direction and strength (aka momentum) of the trend.

 Basics:
 --------
 MACD = EMA12 - EMA26
      = Shortterm  - Long term

 Negative means downtrend, positive means uptrend.


 Details:
 ---------
 It has 2 lines and a directional histogram

 1) MACD Line : Plot of EMA12 - EMA26

 2) Signal Line : "Smoothens" out Noise in (1) by doing EMA_MACD_9d

 With above in mind, when (1) crosses (2) it is a Bullish signal and when it drops below (2) it is a Bearish signal.

 3) Directional Histogram tells you magnitude, how much Bullish or Bearish


 